---
pagination:
  data: collections.photoNaturalOrBuilt
  size: 1
  alias: group
  # Eleventy adds only the FIRST page of a paginated set to collections.all,
  # which the sitemap iterates - so until 3 September 2026 the sitemap listed
  # one archive page per section (the alphabetically first group) and omitted
  # 101 of 296 pages. The sitemap is the only consumer of collections.all.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/natural-or-built/{{ group.slug }}/"
layout: base.njk
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ group.key }}"
  description: "{% if group.key == 'Natural' %}Photographs made in a natural environment — no built works in the landscape, whatever subject may be crossing it.{% elif group.key == 'Altered' %}Photographs of natural ground shaped by human hand: reservoirs, groynes, planted avenues and made paths.{% else %}Photographs of the built world — buildings, bridges, harbour walls and the machines that move through them.{% endif %}"
---
<h1 class="page-title">{{ group.key }}</h1>
<p class="page-intro">
  {% if group.key == "Natural" %}
    A natural environment, which is not the same as a natural subject. Nothing
    built stands in these places — a claim about the ground and the air, not
    about the balloon crossing them, the vehicle parked at the edge of the
    grass, or the Mustang going past.
  {% elif group.key == "Altered" %}
    Natural ground shaped by human hand: water impounded behind a dam, timber
    driven into a beach, birches planted in rows, a path worn out to a tower.
    Neither one thing nor the other, which is usually the point.
  {% else %}
    The built world — buildings, bridges, harbour walls, and the machines that
    move through them.
  {% endif %}
  <a href="/natural-or-built/">Natural or built</a>
</p>
<ul class="gallery-grid">
{% for photo in group.items %}
  <li class="gallery-grid__item">
    <a href="{{ photo.url }}">
      <img src="/images/photos/{{ photo.data.image }}" alt="{{ photo.data.alt }}" loading="lazy" />
      <span class="gallery-grid__caption">{{ photo.data.title }}</span>
    </a>
  </li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
